  "note": "Re-recorded by the Sprint-4 review fixes (2026-09-09). Two precision failures were removed at their root: MLV709's pairing is now scoped to one model (compile() -> its keras.Model(inputs, outputs) -> the layer behind outputs) instead of to a module and an activation family, so neither two builders in one module nor a squeeze-and-excite sigmoid gate is judged an output activation; and MLV121 now requires a holdout to exist (a take/skip pair off the same shuffle, or a subset bound to an evaluation name) instead of firing on `for images, labels in train_ds.take(1)`. `binding_of` gained `exclude`, so `ds = ds.map(...)` / `df = df.dropna()` no longer resolve the right-hand side against the store the same statement is about to write - the tf.data probe went from 2 nodes / 0 edges to 7 / 5 in that binding style and MLV101 fires on the commonest pandas idiom in existence. One program was added, keras_se_gate, carrying the MLV709 and MLV121 false-positive shapes as `forbidden` labels and a rebinding-style tf.data holdout as `expected`: overall recall 0.7143 -> 0.7179, visible 0.6364 -> 0.6410, high+medium 0.6250 -> 0.6316. Unseen is unchanged at 0.5319 and graph fidelity at 0.9065; the new program is marked tuned because the guards were developed against its shapes. Precision stayed 1.0 everywhere. Recall may only ratchet up; a forbidden finding is never tolerated. Regenerate with `python tools/accuracy.py --update-baseline` and say in the commit body which change earned the new number.",
